<title>UK: HTV shares up amid talk United ups stake.</title>
<headline>HTV shares up amid talk United ups stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in HTV Plc rose on Friday as a large trade in the stock at 420p prompted talk that United News &amp; Media Plc had increased its stake, traders said.</p>
<p>HTV shares were up 22-1/2p at 374 by 1323 GMT.  </p>
<p>The trade of 8.3 million shares in HTV was reported at 1241 GMT. Earlier this month United bought a 20 percent stake in HTV from Scottish Television, fuelling talk that it planned a full bid for the company.</p>
<p>Later United confirmed it had bought 8.7 million HTV shares for some 36.7 million stg, taking its stake to 29.9 percent.</p>
<p>United shares were up 12p at 677-1/2 by 1322 GMT while HTV shares wre up 26p at 377-1/2.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
